  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Govcio has $223M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Govcio won 15 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $14.8M. Obligations are down 1.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show a peak in FY23 at $288M and a gradual decline to $223M in FY26. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer, accounting for $213M of obligations. Computer Systems Design Services and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services are the largest markets, with $119M and $93.1M respectively. Current-year totals are partial, and the figures reported are contract obligations except for award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. This profile highlights concentration in a few customers and markets, a modest year-over-year decline, and relatively large average award sizes for the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Govcio's FY2026 to date obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for $213M of Govcio's $223M in FY2026 to date obligations. The Department of the Treasury, the Department of Defense, and the Export-Import Bank of the United States account for much smaller shares at $7.6M, $828K, and $819K respectively. This shows a high customer concentration in one agency."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets are driving Govcio's revenue this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services are the top markets at $119M and $93.1M respectively. Other Computer Related Services contributes $10M. Those three markets together represent the large majority of reported market obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
